  "name": "Camping Paws",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Camping Paws was an annual furry camping event at the Capoxi Dam in Jilotzingo, State of Mexico, about an hour and a half from Mexico City, organized by Capital Fur. It grew from a small group of Mexico City furries who organized their own camp in mid-2017 and then opened it to everyone each year. Registration included round-trip transport from Mexico City, food, lodging, a shirt, a commemorative cup and a badge, and activities included outdoor and lounge games, a campfire and a night party. The last edition was held in 2019, and the planned 2020 camp did not take place.",
